.TH BIGINTSUB 3 "2026-09-25" "BigNums 3" "Library Functions Manual"
.nr HY 0
.ds AD l
.SH NAME
bigIntAdd, bigIntSub, bigIntCmp, bigIntCmpAbs \- add, subtract or compare signed integers
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <bignums.h>

int bigIntSub(BigInt *result, const BigInt *a, const BigInt *b);
int bigIntAdd(BigInt *result, const BigInt *a, const BigInt *b);
int bigIntCmp(const BigInt *a, const BigInt *b);
int bigIntCmpAbs(const BigInt *a, const BigInt *b);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Add stores a plus b and Sub stores a minus b, for any combination of signs.
Negative results are supported; zero is always positive. The output may alias
either or both inputs and must be initialized.
Cmp compares signed values; CmpAbs compares magnitudes ignoring sign.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Add and Sub return 0, -1 for allocation failure, or INT_MAX
for an unrepresentable size. Errors leave output unchanged.
Cmp and CmpAbs return -1, 0 or +1 as comparison values.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bignums (3),
.BR bignums (7)
